<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peace of Okahandja</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1870">1870</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Peace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/okahandja">Okahandja</a> was the settlement of 1870, negotiated with the help of German missionaries, that ended a decade of war between the Herero under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharero">Maharero</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oorlam">Oorlam</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afrikaners">Afrikaners</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-jonker-afrikaner">Jan Jonker Afrikaner</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">Namibia</a>. It confirmed Herero independence and was followed by a period of relative peace in the region.</p></div>
